      "text": "\"Inspect this Python service in read-only mode. Do not modify files. The active HTTP entry point is service.routes.dispatch.\n\nWhich IDs does active GET /orders return in input order for principal={\\\"id\\\":\\\"u1\\\",\\\"tenant\\\":\\\"north\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"member\\\"} and repository rows=[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"o1\\\",\\\"tenant\\\":\\\"north\\\",\\\"owner\\\":\\\"u1\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"draft\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"o2\\\",\\\"tenant\\\":\\\"north\\\",\\\"owner\\\":\\\"u2\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"draft\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"o3\\\",\\\"tenant\\\":\\\"north\\\",\\\"owner\\\":\\\"u2\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"published\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"o4\\\",\\\"tenant\\\":\\\"south\\\",\\\"owner\\\":\\\"u1\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"published\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"o5\\\",\\\"tenant\\\":\\\"north\\\",\\\"owner\\\":\\\"u1\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"deleted\\\"}]? Identify the authorization function and the function that excludes deleted rows.\n\nReturn one JSON object, with no Markdown fences or prose outside it. Use {\\\"answer\\\": ..., \\\"evidence\\\": [{\\\"path\\\": ..., \\\"symbol\\\": ..., \\\"line\\\": ..., \\\"quote\\\": ...}]}. The answer object must have exactly these fields, whose descriptions follow.\n{\\\"ids\\\": \\\"ordered list of order IDs\\\", \\\"authorization\\\": \\\"fully qualified function\\\", \\\"deleted_filter\\\": \\\"fully qualified function\\\"}\nProvide at most eight evidence entries. Each path must be relative to this directory. Use the local function name, Class.method, or top-level assignment name for symbol. Use a one-based line number and copy the entire source line exactly, including indentation. Cite the specific statements supporting every answer field. For absence of a route, cite the active registration table and missing-route branch.\"",
